\begin{bgproofidea}[title={The factorial makes derivative matching exact}]
The term
\[
\frac{f^{(n)}(a)}{n!}(x-a)^n
\]
vanishes under fewer than \(n\) derivatives at \(x=a\), and after \(n\) derivatives contributes exactly \(f^{(n)}(a)\). This triangular structure determines every coefficient.
\end{bgproofidea}

