\section*{Common Errors in Power and Taylor Series}
\begin{bgmistake}[title={Forgetting endpoints}]The Ratio Test determines the open interval but is generally inconclusive at its endpoints.\end{bgmistake}
\begin{bgmistake}[title={Dropping the center}]A Taylor series about \(a\) uses powers of \(x-a\), not powers of \(x\).\end{bgmistake}
\begin{bgmistake}[title={Claiming equality without controlling the remainder}]A formal Taylor series is not automatically the original function.\end{bgmistake}
